<article class="publication-body"><p>Freshdesk is worth considering when a support team needs a structured ticket workflow without assembling separate tools for the inbox, customer portal, knowledge base and reporting. Its main buying risk is not a missing headline feature. It is whether the selected plan, AI usage rules and export options match the work your agents actually do. This review uses official product, pricing and help documentation checked October 29, 2026. It is documentation-based research, not a hands-on account test.</p>
<section class="answer"><strong>Short verdict:</strong> Freshdesk is a sensible shortlist choice for email-first support teams that need ticket ownership, a shared inbox, self-service content and reporting. Compare alternatives if you mainly need a small shared inbox, CRM-led service or a specialized ecommerce workflow. Before buying, confirm whether your team needs Freshdesk or the separate Freshdesk Omni product.</section>
<details class="publication-mobile-toc"><summary>On this page</summary><nav aria-label="Mobile table of contents"><a href="#verdict">Verdict</a><a href="#product-scope">Product scope</a><a href="#pricing">Pricing and add-ons</a><a href="#strengths">Where it fits</a><a href="#limits">Limits and risks</a><a href="#migration">Data export and migration</a><a href="#best-fit">Best-fit teams</a><a href="#evaluation">How to evaluate it</a><a href="#faq">Freshdesk FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Sources</a></nav></details>
<h2 id="product-scope">What product is being reviewed?</h2><p>Freshworks distinguishes Freshdesk from Freshdesk Omni. Its onboarding guide describes Freshdesk as email-first, while Freshdesk Omni supports a broader set of channels such as email, chat and social interactions in a unified inbox. The public pricing page reviewed here is titled Freshdesk. If your team needs omnichannel service, verify the exact product and quote before comparing plans.</p><p>The Freshdesk pricing page lists ticketing, shared inbox, customer portal, knowledge base, standard analytics and reporting, threads and tasks, and roles and permissions on Growth. Pro adds multilingual help desk, custom dashboards, intelligent routing, multiple SLA policies and external collaborators. Enterprise adds Freddy AI Insights, skill-based routing, sandbox, audit logs and domain/IP controls. These are vendor-published features, not claims from an independent product test.</p>
<h2 id="pricing">Pricing and add-ons checked October 29, 2026</h2><p>The official pricing page displays the following annual-billing prices. It also includes a Monthly/Annually selector, so do not treat these annual rates as month-to-month prices. <a href="https://www.freshworks.com/freshdesk/pricing/">Confirm current billing and plan terms on the official page.</a></p><div class="publication-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Plan</th><th>Published price</th><th>Notable features</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Growth</th><td>US$19 per agent/month billed annually. <a href="https://www.freshworks.com/freshdesk/pricing/">Official pricing, checked October 29, 2026.</a></td><td>Ticketing, shared inbox, customer portal, knowledge base and standard reporting.</td></tr><tr><th>Pro</th><td>US$55 per agent/month billed annually. <a href="https://www.freshworks.com/freshdesk/pricing/">Official pricing, checked October 29, 2026.</a></td><td>Multilingual help desk, custom dashboards, intelligent routing and multiple SLA policies.</td></tr><tr><th>Enterprise</th><td>US$89 per agent/month billed annually. <a href="https://www.freshworks.com/freshdesk/pricing/">Official pricing, checked October 29, 2026.</a></td><td>Freddy AI Insights, skill-based routing, sandbox and audit logs.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The page offers a 14-day trial that starts with Enterprise access. It does not list a permanent free plan. Trial and plan details were checked October 29, 2026 on the <a href="https://www.freshworks.com/freshdesk/pricing/">official pricing page</a>.</p><p>AI usage needs its own budget. The table lists the first 500 Freddy AI Agent sessions as included and additional sessions at US$49 per 100. It does not clearly state the renewal period for the included allowance, so ask Freshworks to confirm how the 500 sessions are counted and when the allowance resets. Pro and Enterprise list Freddy AI Copilot at US$29 per agent/month as an add-on. Day passes, connector app tasks and MCP actions also have separate charges. These amounts were checked October 29, 2026 on the <a href="https://www.freshworks.com/freshdesk/pricing/">official pricing page</a>.</p>
<h2 id="strengths">Where Freshdesk fits well</h2><h3>Ticket ownership and collaboration</h3><p>A shared inbox is useful, but the value of a help desk comes from making ownership visible. Freshdesk lists ticketing, shared inbox, threads and tasks on Growth. A team can keep the customer-facing reply separate from internal discussion and assign work without relying only on mailbox labels. The workflow still needs clear group names, priority rules and an owner for unassigned tickets.</p><h3>Self-service alongside support</h3><p>The public plan table lists a customer portal and knowledge base on all three displayed tiers. This helps teams publish answers to repeated questions and gives customers a route to submit requests. The value depends on the quality of the articles and whether agents keep them current. A knowledge base with old screenshots or unclear steps can create more tickets instead of reducing them.</p><h3>Reporting and routing can scale with the team</h3><p>Growth lists standard analytics and reporting; Pro adds custom dashboards, intelligent routing and multiple SLA policies; Enterprise adds skill-based routing and audit logs. This tier structure is useful when the team can identify a specific reporting or governance gap. It is less useful to pay for a feature before the workflow has a defined owner and a clear reason to use it.</p>
<h2 id="limits">Limits and risks to check</h2><h3>AI usage is not the same as an agent seat</h3><p>The included 500-session allowance and extra-session charge should be treated as a separate meter. Ask how a session is counted, whether the allowance renews, and what happens when the team reaches it. If you plan to use Copilot, include its per-agent add-on in the budget. Do not assume an AI feature is unlimited because the help desk plan is billed per agent.</p><h3>Advanced controls require the right tier</h3><p>Custom dashboards, intelligent routing and multiple SLA policies are listed on Pro, while Enterprise adds skill-based routing, sandbox and audit logs. If one of these is a hard requirement, compare the full tier rather than the Growth entry price. If your workflow only needs basic ticket ownership, the higher tier may add cost without improving the outcome.</p><h3>Freshdesk and Freshdesk Omni are different product choices</h3><p>Freshworks describes Freshdesk as email-first and Freshdesk Omni as the multichannel option. A team that needs chat or social channels should verify the product, plan and included channels before buying. Do not assume the Freshdesk price table automatically describes an Omni deployment.</p><h3>Export coverage needs a test</h3><p>Freshdesk's official ticket export guide describes filtered ticket exports and limitations. A ticket-list export should not be treated as a full account archive with every conversation, archived ticket, attachment, custom field, report and automation. This matters most when switching systems or keeping an independent backup.</p>
<h2 id="migration">Data export and migration</h2><p>Before moving to Freshdesk or leaving it, inventory the records and configuration you must preserve: tickets, comments, attachments, contacts, organizations, custom fields, macros, rules, knowledge articles, reports and user permissions. The <a href="https://support.freshdesk.com/support/solutions/articles/225158">official ticket export guide</a>, checked October 29, 2026, explains the list-export path. Test the account-level export option separately if you need a wider archive.</p><p>Run a sample export and check record counts, timestamps, attachments and older cases. For an inbound migration, map source fields to Freshdesk fields before importing all records. Rebuild routing and SLA logic intentionally; a destination platform may import messages without reproducing the rules that acted on them. Keep the source system available until the new workflow has passed a realistic test.</p>
<h2 id="best-fit">Who should choose Freshdesk?</h2><h3>Good fit</h3><ul><li>Email-first teams that need clear ticket ownership and shared inbox collaboration.</li><li>Support operations that use a customer portal and knowledge base.</li><li>Managers who need standard reporting today and may need custom dashboards or routing later.</li><li>Teams willing to measure AI usage and confirm add-on terms before scaling.</li></ul><h3>Compare an alternative when</h3><ul><li>You only need a simple shared inbox and the free tier of another product meets your volume.</li><li>Support must be deeply tied to CRM records, sales workflows or a broader customer platform.</li><li>Your business needs ecommerce-specific order context and ticket-volume billing.</li><li>You cannot accept unclear export scope or have strict portability requirements that are not verified.</li></ul><p>The <a href="/freshdesk/alternatives/">Freshdesk alternatives guide</a> compares Zendesk, Help Scout, Zoho Desk, Intercom, Front, HubSpot Service Hub, Gorgias and Salesforce Service Cloud by workflow. The <a href="/compare/freshdesk-vs-help-scout/">Freshdesk vs Help Scout comparison</a> focuses on shared inbox needs, free access, AI meters and migration.</p>
<h2 id="evaluation">How to evaluate Freshdesk before paying</h2><ol><li>Pick five real support cases, including a normal question, an escalation, an attachment-heavy issue, a reopened ticket and an ambiguous request.</li><li>Build the smallest workflow that covers those cases and check assignment, internal notes, replies and resolution.</li><li>Publish one knowledge article and test it as a customer without agent access.</li><li>Review the reporting available on the plan you would buy, not the highest plan shown in a demo.</li><li>Estimate AI sessions, add-ons and the usage period of the included allowance with Freshworks.</li><li>Export sample tickets and check what is missing before relying on the data for migration or backup.</li><li>Calculate the annual cost for the actual number of agents, then confirm tax, billing and product SKU at checkout.</li></ol><p>This approach produces a better decision than relying on a feature list. It also creates a checklist that can be repeated if you compare Freshdesk with another help desk later.</p>
<h2 id="faq">Freshdesk review FAQ</h2><h3>Is Freshdesk free?</h3><p>The current Freshdesk pricing page does not list a permanent free plan. It offers a 14-day trial that starts with Enterprise access.</p><h3>What is the starting Freshdesk price?</h3><p>The official pricing page checked October 29, 2026 lists Growth at US$19 per agent/month billed annually, with Pro at US$55 and Enterprise at US$89.</p><h3>Are Freshdesk AI sessions unlimited?</h3><p>No. The pricing table lists the first 500 Freddy AI Agent sessions as included and extra sessions at US$49 per 100, but it does not clearly state the renewal period. Confirm the allowance with Freshworks.</p><h3>Can I export all Freshdesk ticket history?</h3><p>Do not assume a ticket-list export is a complete account archive. The official export guide describes filtered ticket exports and limitations, so test the account-level export path if you need full history.</p>
